WEBVTT

00:04.650 --> 00:07.387
This video walks through how escape works at Boonesboro

00:07.387 --> 00:10.575
Quarry. One thing first. The maps you'll see here

00:10.575 --> 00:13.412
are simplified traces of the Boonesboro escapeway

00:13.412 --> 00:16.975
maps, one for each level. Escape routes change

00:16.975 --> 00:19.850
as mining moves, so the map posted at the mine

00:19.850 --> 00:22.450
always governs. Your instructor will show you the

00:22.450 --> 00:25.288
current map and walk the actual escapeways with

00:25.288 --> 00:27.250
you during your mine-site training.

00:28.380 --> 00:31.180
Boonesboro is an underground limestone mine worked

00:31.180 --> 00:33.755
room-and-pillar, and it has three levels.

00:33.755 --> 00:36.893
Active mining is on Level 2 and Level 3.

00:36.893 --> 00:39.843
The primary crusher is on Level 2, and the crushed

00:39.843 --> 00:42.943
rock is conveyed outside to the surface plant.

00:42.943 --> 00:45.855
Level 1 holds stockpiles and the mine shop.

00:46.974 --> 00:49.236
Escape starts before you go underground.

00:49.236 --> 00:51.874
At Boonesboro, you check in on the covered tag

00:51.874 --> 00:55.262
board outside every shift, and visitors and contractors

00:55.262 --> 00:57.736
use their own check-in board in the breakroom.

00:57.736 --> 01:00.049
Then know which level you're working on today,

01:00.049 --> 01:03.474
one, two, or three, and your work area on that

01:03.474 --> 01:06.299
level. Your escape route depends on both.

01:06.299 --> 01:08.774
It's the first line on your Boonesboro emergency

01:08.774 --> 01:09.524
card.

01:10.681 --> 01:12.793
Here's what to look for on an escape map.

01:12.793 --> 01:15.293
The plan's maps show the escape routes,

01:15.293 --> 01:18.006
the direction the main air flows, where the phones

01:18.006 --> 01:21.006
are, and where the main fans, fan controls,

01:21.006 --> 01:23.343
fire doors and ventilation doors are.

01:23.343 --> 01:25.718
Find the "you are here" point first.

01:25.718 --> 01:28.706
Then follow the escape routes back toward the portal,

01:28.706 --> 01:31.094
and notice which way the air is moving.

01:32.226 --> 01:35.001
Air direction matters in a fire. Smoke travels

01:35.001 --> 01:37.826
with the air. That's also why stench gas,

01:37.826 --> 01:40.889
released at the intake fan, reaches every working

01:40.889 --> 01:41.676
area.

01:45.004 --> 01:47.992
Every underground mine must have at least two separate

01:47.992 --> 01:51.017
escapeways to the surface from its lowest levels,

01:51.017 --> 01:53.792
placed so that damage to one doesn't block the

01:53.792 --> 01:56.867
other. At Boonesboro that means from Level 3 and

01:56.867 --> 01:59.917
Level 2 back up and out. You need to know both:

01:59.917 --> 02:03.029
the primary escapeway, which you'd normally use,

02:03.029 --> 02:05.554
and the secondary, for when the primary is blocked

02:05.554 --> 02:08.717
by smoke, fire, or a fall of ground.

02:08.717 --> 02:11.454
On the Boonesboro maps, both are marked with green

02:11.454 --> 02:15.042
arrows. A P in the arrow's circle means primary,

02:15.042 --> 02:17.117
and an S means secondary.

02:18.238 --> 02:20.488
If someone is hurt underground, they come out by

02:20.488 --> 02:23.976
the primary escapeway. Any miner can call for help,

02:23.976 --> 02:26.963
and any miner can meet the ambulance at the portal.

02:28.096 --> 02:31.084
Don't just look at them on paper. Walk both escapeways

02:31.084 --> 02:32.934
from your level with your instructor,

02:32.934 --> 02:35.646
and again any time your work area moves.

02:35.646 --> 02:38.546
Notice landmarks: the crusher on Level 2,

02:38.546 --> 02:41.621
conveyors, intersections, and where the route changes

02:41.621 --> 02:44.334
level. In smoke you may not see much,

02:44.334 --> 02:47.171
so the more familiar the route is, the better.

02:47.171 --> 02:49.946
Underground traffic still moves at up to twenty-five

02:49.946 --> 02:52.459
miles per hour, so in a normal shift,

02:52.459 --> 02:55.084
travel the escapeways the same careful way you

02:55.084 --> 02:57.596
travel every other road underground.

02:58.714 --> 03:01.327
Escape routes have to be inspected regularly,

03:01.327 --> 03:04.227
kept travelable, and marked with signs that clearly

03:04.227 --> 03:06.677
show the way out. On the mine maps,

03:06.677 --> 03:09.352
escapeways are marked with green arrows.

03:09.352 --> 03:12.189
Underground, the primary escapeway is marked with

03:12.189 --> 03:14.764
white reflectors on the ribs, and the secondary

03:14.764 --> 03:17.927
escapeway with blue reflectors, along with reflective

03:17.927 --> 03:21.126
signs and arrows. Learn them, and watch for them

03:21.126 --> 03:23.939
every time you travel. Never block an escapeway

03:23.939 --> 03:26.314
with equipment, stockpiled material,

03:26.314 --> 03:28.989
or anything else. If a sign is missing,

03:28.989 --> 03:31.589
or a route is blocked, report it right away.

03:32.729 --> 03:35.379
Boonesboro has a written escape and evacuation

03:35.379 --> 03:38.191
plan. Parts of the mine map showing escape routes

03:38.191 --> 03:40.641
are posted underground where people gather,

03:40.641 --> 03:44.004
such as shops and lunch areas. At Boonesboro,

03:44.004 --> 03:47.441
maps are posted in the breakroom and on every level:

03:47.441 --> 03:50.066
in the shop on Level 1, at the primary crusher

03:50.066 --> 03:53.554
MCC on Level 2, and on Level 3 between the ramps

03:53.554 --> 03:56.429
at the porta john. Stop and read the map whenever

03:56.429 --> 03:59.479
you pass one. Find where you are, then trace both

03:59.479 --> 04:00.441
ways out.

04:03.758 --> 04:06.521
At Boonesboro, the underground fire warning is

04:06.521 --> 04:09.583
stench gas, released into the intake fan so it

04:09.583 --> 04:11.833
travels through the mine with the air.

04:11.833 --> 04:14.471
You may also get a warning by radio or by strobe

04:14.471 --> 04:17.383
lights. The emergency lights at the mine entrance

04:17.383 --> 04:20.483
are used for evacuation, and before blasting.

04:20.483 --> 04:22.271
When you get any of those warnings,

04:22.271 --> 04:24.733
don't wait to confirm it. Warn the people around

04:24.733 --> 04:27.071
you and start out by your escapeway.

04:27.071 --> 04:30.346
On the CB, the scale house is on channel 30 and

04:30.346 --> 04:32.721
the yard loaders are on channel 19.

04:33.848 --> 04:36.498
At the first sign of smoke, a CO alarm,

04:36.498 --> 04:40.036
or stench gas, put on your W65 self-rescuer right

04:40.036 --> 04:42.811
away. The air it gives you gets hot and dry,

04:42.811 --> 04:45.473
and that's normal. Keep it on until you reach fresh

04:45.473 --> 04:46.861
air on the surface.

04:47.991 --> 04:50.078
Once you're out, go straight to your gathering

04:50.078 --> 04:52.703
point and report to the person in charge so you're

04:52.703 --> 04:55.228
counted. Don't go back in for tools,

04:55.228 --> 04:58.266
a vehicle, or a coworker unless the person in charge

04:58.266 --> 05:01.241
tells you to. At Boonesboro, the gathering points

05:01.241 --> 05:03.778
are the tag board and a designated area behind

05:03.778 --> 05:07.053
the mine, outside the 22 North escapeway.

05:08.193 --> 05:11.118
There's no designated refuge chamber at Boonesboro,

05:11.118 --> 05:13.755
so the plan is to get out. That's why knowing both

05:13.755 --> 05:16.380
escapeways from your level matters so much.

05:16.380 --> 05:18.680
You'll practice it in evacuation drills,

05:18.680 --> 05:21.205
which are held at least every six months.

05:22.334 --> 05:25.597
If smoke, fire, or fallen rock blocks the primary

05:25.597 --> 05:29.022
escapeway, turn around and take the secondary.

05:29.022 --> 05:31.022
Don't try to push through heavy smoke if there's

05:31.022 --> 05:33.509
another way. Stay together with the people around

05:33.509 --> 05:37.497
you, keep your W65 on, and keep moving toward fresh

05:37.497 --> 05:40.922
air. If you get turned around, stop at an intersection

05:40.922 --> 05:42.997
and look for the direction signs before you go

05:42.997 --> 05:43.622
on.

05:44.757 --> 05:47.569
To sum up for Boonesboro. Tag in, and know your

05:47.569 --> 05:50.744
level and work area. Know the primary and secondary

05:50.744 --> 05:53.344
escapeway from where you work, and read the posted

05:53.344 --> 05:57.294
maps. At the first warning, put on your W65 and

05:57.294 --> 05:59.869
head out. Then go to the gathering point and get

05:59.869 --> 06:02.544
counted. Fill in your emergency card with your

06:02.544 --> 06:05.357
instructor before your first shift underground.

06:06.482 --> 06:09.645
Remember: your site's plans and procedures always

06:09.645 --> 06:11.145
override this video.
